# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in from your Supabase project's
# Settings → API page. Restart the dev server after changing these — Expo inlines
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time, so a running Metro will keep serving the old values.
#
# The anon key is a *publishable* key and is meant to ship inside the app; it grants
# nothing on its own. Access is decided by row-level security policies on the server.
# Never put the `service_role` key here — that one bypasses RLS entirely.
#
# Leave both unset and the app runs exactly as it did before: no account, no network,
# everything local. `supabase` is null and every caller degrades to "unconfigured".

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
